    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Similarly, the average proportion of pairwise mismatches in sequences of length L is given by $ \\Pi/L $. This quantity does have an established symbol, namely $ \\pi = \\Pi/L $, and it is called the nucleotide diversity <sup>[506]</sup>. Because L is a constant, the mean and variance of $ \\pi $ are given by $$ E(\\pi)=E(\\Pi)/L\\quad V(\\pi)=V(\\Pi)/L^{2} $$",
      "source_page": 190,
      "source_pages": [
        190
      ],
